        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most large dogs, the <strong class="text-white">Dog Runner Revolution Pro</strong> is the
            place to start: about 71 by 18 inches of running surface, a 3.5 HP motor and powered
            incline, for around $2,450. Giant breeds too long for that need the 84-inch
            <strong class="text-white">Jog A Dog DC7</strong>, older dogs on a vet’s programme the Ortho
            Pro, and athletic dogs that want to run a Dog Trotter slatmill.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whichever you choose, measure your dog against the running surface first, speak to your vet
            before the first session, and never tether or leave a dog on a moving belt. For smaller
            dogs, see our
            <a href="/best-dog-treadmills/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">general dog treadmill roundup</a>.
          </p>
